ackages.`, hint_r1_good: `Strong read. You found most of the omissions that matter for the counter.`, hint_r2_unethical: `Threats and bluffs turn negotiation into confrontation. HR will call legal and the offer will tighten. Remove these from your leverage map.`, hint_r2_good: `Clean leverage map. These are the assets you can trade for a better exit.`, hint_r3_threat: `A threatening tone will cost you. HR reads threats as escalation and tightens the offer. Rewrite in firm but professional language.`, hint_r3_lawyer: `Package value above €30,000 and no lawyer engaged. A €1,500 review typically returns 5 to 20 times the fee. Reconsider.`, hint_r3_statute: `No statutory anchor in the ask. HR will read this as fishing. Anchor on 33 days per year of service under Spanish law for a much stronger counter.`, hint_r3_good: `Well-anchored counter. This is how Director-level separations move 30 to 60 percent above the initial offer.`, hint_r4_sign: `You signed away everything you negotiated. This is the most common outcome and the most expensive one.`, hint_r4_noCounsel: `Escalating to legal without counsel is a public declaration of intent with nothing to back it. You gave up leverage and credibility in one move.`, hint_r4_held: `You held the floor calmly. HR knows you have done your homework. The enhanced portion is yours.`, hint_r4_general: `Separation negotiations reward patience. The 7-day window is theatre. Counters that hold typically close within 2 to 3 weeks.`, col_round: `Round`, col_package: `Package Value`, col_credibility: `Credibility`, insight_strong: `Strong outcome. You moved the package 30 percent or more above the initial offer — consistent with well-prepared Director-level counters.`, insight_weak: `The package barely moved. Most of the gap was recoverable value you left with the company.`, insight_lawyer: `You signed a material package without engaging counsel. Future separations of this size warrant a paid legal review as a rule, not an exception.`, insig